                           <th>Conclusion and Recommendations based on this report and previous findings known to us</th>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                           <td>The patient’s estimated glomerular filtration rate (eGFR) is mildly decreased, consistent with age-related decline in renal function but still within the range for stage 2 chronic kidney disease. No acute kidney injury is indicated. Regular monitoring of renal function is recommended, especially if there are comorbidities or nephrotoxic medications.</td>
